  "system": {
    "slug": "the-illusive-man",
    "details": {
      "level": {
        "value": 14
      },
      "publicNotes": "<p>The Illusive Man, born Jack Harper, is the shadowy founder and leader of Cerberus. He controls a vast interstellar organization from an undisclosed location, orchestrating human advancement through methods that mainstream civilization would never sanction. Brilliant, ruthless, and driven by genuine conviction rather than simple villainy, he is one of the most dangerous humans in the galaxy. He has been experimented on with Reaper technology, granting him powerful abilities while gradually compromising his free will.</p><p><strong>Indoctrination (aura, 60 ft):</strong> Any non-Cerberus humanoid who starts their turn within the aura must succeed on a DC 32 Will save or be Confused for 1 round.</p><p><strong>Reaper Touch (2 actions):</strong> The Illusive Man unleashes Reaper-enhanced biotic energy. One target within 60 feet takes 5d10+10 force damage (DC 32 Will for half) and must succeed on a DC 32 Fortitude save or be Stunned 2.</p><p><strong>This is Not Over (reaction):</strong> When reduced to 0 HP, the Illusive Man makes one final Reaper Touch before collapsing. This uses a reaction.</p>",
      "privateNotes": "",
      "publication": {
        "title": "Mass Effect Compendium",
        "authors": "nscarpinatodev",
        "license": "ORC",
        "remaster": true
      },
      "languages": {
        "value": [],
        "details": ""
      },
      "blurb": "Founder and leader of Cerberus; brilliant strategist partially indoctrinated by Reaper technology."
